From 53be90a182bd02792bab6904bf41429e64285116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:01:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] split screen: fix pane bleed, aiming inside the pane, player
 2 combat and viewmodel

- gx: R_DrawWorld reset the scissor to the whole screen in the middle of a
  view, so geometry spilled into the other half. Restore the view's scissor.
- Wiimote pointer, crosshair, shot direction and viewmodel lean now work
  inside player 1's pane (FOV and aspect of the pane); player 2's Nunchuk
  pointer is measured in its own pane.
- Player 2: v.fixangle was never acknowledged by the fake client, so the
  engine ignored its usercmd angles (no aim, no damage, no use). Clear it and
  adopt the angles the game asked for.
- Player 2 first person weapon: sniff svc_weaponanim sent to the fake client,
  lend clgame.viewent to the renderer for player 2's view (RF_SPLIT_VIEWMODEL).
- New command wii_split_info and a warning when player 2 gets input but does
  not move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011GqZpE1Ju6sDf6Gef1CAAi
